<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongkut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1868</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rama IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mongkut, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> IV of Siam, reigned from 1851 to 1868. Before his accession he spent 27 years as a Buddhist monk, founding the reformist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhammayuttika-nikaya">Thammayut order</a> and studying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, English and Western science. As king he signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bowring-treaty">Bowring Treaty</a> of 1855 and similar treaties that opened Siam to Western trade, and he died of malaria caught on an expedition to observe a solar eclipse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongkut.jpg" alt="Mongkut" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Thomson · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_King_of_Siam_MET_DP-573-001_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
